# Post-install reminders for Emoji Nook — the two things easy to miss
#
# (c) Copyright 2026 Liminal HQ, Scott Morris
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT

_emoji_nook_notes() {
  cat <<'EOF'

==> Emoji Nook: two setup steps are easy to miss.

  1. Emoji injection works best with ydotool, but installing the package
     alone is not enough — it also needs the input group and its user
     service running:

       sudo usermod -aG input "$USER"
       # log out and back in, then:
       systemctl --user enable --now ydotool

     Without this, injection silently falls back to wtype (does not work
     on GNOME) or xdotool (X11/XWayland only).

  2. On GNOME Shell, the tray icon will not appear without an AppIndicator
     host extension — GNOME removed native tray support in 3.26. Install
     and enable gnome-shell-extension-appindicator (already listed as an
     optional dependency). Not needed on KDE or other desktops with
     native tray support.

EOF
}

post_install() {
  _emoji_nook_notes
}

post_upgrade() {
  _emoji_nook_notes
}
